      "writtenOn": "2020-11-30T16:03:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this scenario, is it that we don\u0027t have the sink caps in sink ready, or do we need to process them again when we start up as a sink?  Since they\u0027re stored, I would expect us to only need to re-read the sink capabilities as we start up and there wouldn\u0027t be a need for additional PD traffic.",
      "revId": "ba655d6008da1b2eb943af4f4c52b46c1b0702eb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a2af315f_f77209f4",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2748,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-01T00:25:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure; pe_invalidate_explicit_contract() explicitly clears the \"FRS enable\" flag during a PRS, but is there a reason to do so? A conservative reading of the spec says that a PRS (or FRS) includes a soft reset of the PE (6.3.10), but 8.3.3.18.9 says partner sink capabilities are given to the DPM so a PE reset wouldn\u0027t clear them.\n\nThat seems to suggest that we can skip clearing the FRS flag on PRS and avoid looking at sink caps again. If I\u0027m wrong and we do need to clear it, then inspecting stored sink caps by breaking FRS configuration out of pe_dr_get_sink_cap_run() seems okay too. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "3c19178f_763b207a",
      "revId": "ba655d6008da1b2eb943af4f4c52b46c1b0702eb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b158012_8a534d92",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2748,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-01T00:37:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should probably only be enabling FRS detection in the HW when we\u0027re a sink to reduce our likelihood of false positive detection while we\u0027re sourcing.  I definitely missed thinking through that case when expanding the sink caps retrieval.\n\nCould we enable FRS either:\n- when we get the sink caps as a sink and see FRS support OR\n- when we start up as a sink and have sink caps indicating FRS support\n\nAnd then we should probably disable it when going back to sourcing, if that happens for some reason.\n\nFor when our explicit contract is invalidated, I think we can assume the partner sink capabilities will remain the same over hard resets and swaps.  I would be somewhat surprised if they changed in these cases, but everyone reads the spec differently so we could see some partners doing this.",
      "parentUuid": "a2af315f_f77209f4",
      "revId": "ba655d6008da1b2eb943af4f4c52b46c1b0702eb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f5070eb_ce71c645",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2748,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-01T01:29:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e when we get the sink caps as a sink and see FRS support\n\nWe will often connect initially as source and get sink caps then later become the sink, so that\u0027s what this change is currently doing: ensuring we get sink caps as a sink so FRS gets enabled. Though we don\u0027t currently check whether we\u0027re a sink to set the FRS flag.\n\n\u003e when we start up as a sink and have sink caps indicating FRS support\n\nIf we were a sink on initial startup then we won\u0027t have sink caps indicating FRS support until DPM_REQUEST_GET_SINK_CAPS is handled in pe_snk_ready_run(). We\u0027d have to evaluate sink caps in pe_snk_ready_entry() to ensure we notice if sink caps aren\u0027t already known.\n\nThis would mean we want to have pe_snk_ready_entry() first check that sink caps are present and then evaluate them to enable FRS if appropriate, doing nothing if they\u0027re not known. Evaluation can be skipped if FRS is already enabled.\npe_snk_ready_run() will handle DPM_REQUEST_GET_SINK_CAPS and ultimately trigger pe_snk_ready_entry() when transitioning back to PE_SNK_Ready from PE_DR_SNK_Get_Sink_Cap to evaluate caps once they\u0027re known.",
      "parentUuid": "9b158012_8a534d92",
      "revId": "ba655d6008da1b2eb943af4f4c52b46c1b0702eb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3cb01ec_17be65f3",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
